    "proof_nodes": [
      {
        "id": "P1",
        "text": "For each finite exponent q>=1, linear Gaussian projections form a continuous linear Lq-valued map. Prove smoothness of the nth power simultaneously in every finite q, using continuous Holder multiplication L^(2q) times L^(2q) into Lq for the successor."
      },
      {
        "id": "P2",
        "text": "Polynomial addition and scalar multiplication assemble the smooth L2 map. Almost-everywhere representatives establish literal membership and identify this map with the displayed toLp map."
      },
      {
        "id": "P3",
        "text": "Specialize to the real image of the integer Hermite polynomial. The toLp representative theorem gives the almost-everywhere identity; lower C-infinity to C2."
      },
      {
        "id": "P4",
        "text": "Expand the finite L2 inner product bilinearly. The existing exact mixed Gaussian Hermite product identity annihilates unequal degrees and gives j! <w,z>^j on the diagonal. No new orthogonality proof is introduced."
      },
      {
        "id": "P5",
        "text": "Finite addition of constant scalar multiples preserves global C2."
      }
    ],
    "private_helper": {
      "name": "smooth_power_ridge",
      "module": "AutoSamplingTheory/TechnicalLemmas/Probability/GaussianPolynomialRidgeSmooth.lean",
      "public_owner": "AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Probability.GaussianPolynomialRidgeSmooth.standard_gaussian_polynomial_ridge_L2_smooth",
      "reachable": true,
      "reason": "Directly invoked in the monomial branch. Its simultaneous finite-q induction uses Holder multiplication L^(2q) times L^(2q) into Lq, not L2 times L2 into L2.",
      "credit": "Whole-module implementation coverage only; no separate public theorem credit."
    },
    "public_inventory": {
      "definitions": 2,
      "theorems": 5,
      "private_helpers": 1
    },
    "definition_boundary": "Actual Hermite L2 quotient classes and literal finite sums, not arbitrary features with assumed Gram laws.",
    "parent_boundary": "The existing mixed Gaussian Hermite product theorem is reused with both unit-direction hypotheses; this review does not re-audit its proof.",
    "seal_boundary": "Current admission of existing proofs; no retrospective pre-proof seal or historical authorship is invented."
  },
  "semantic_boundaries": [
    "The polynomial theorem quantifies a family of MemLp proofs after E,p and proves C-infinity in the actual L2 norm over all E. Membership is a conclusion, not a hidden assumption; no unit or quantitative bound appears.",
    "The approved definition body chooses membership witnesses for the literal real coefficient image of the integer Hermite polynomial, then forms its toLp class. Proof irrelevance fixes that value; no arbitrary feature or Gram premise is introduced.",
    "The body is the literal finite scalar sum in the same L2 carrier. Empty support, degree zero and arbitrary signed or zero real coefficients remain allowed; the representative elaboration follows finite linearity.",
    "The class map is C2 on all ambient E, by the exact polynomial specialization and lowering C-infinity. No sphere restriction or additional regularity assumption is inserted.",
    "For each j,w separately, the coerced representative equals the literal Hermite ridge almost everywhere. Neither every-point equality nor a common exceptional set for all w is asserted. The repaired smoothness dependency remains in the reader.",
    "Both actual directions must be unit. The same S,c occur in both factors; the diagonal is j! c(j)^2 times the correlation power. Signed and endpoint correlations, empty S and degree zero are allowed; no independence or ambient nonunit Gram extension is assumed.",
    "Finite sums of constant scalar multiples preserve C2 of the actual class maps on all E. No unit, coefficient positivity, normalization or infinite-series convergence condition is inserted."
  ],
